What it does: an opt-in oracle parameter `mitm-prime-batch:m=2,layout=lines` (default `map`,
every recorded run) puts the batched pair table and the relation guard in line tables
(eight u64 words per 64-byte line, home line a pure function of the key) and turns the lane
round's touch loop into software prefetches (prefetcht0 on x86-64; the old demand read
elsewhere).  Default-layout code paths are unchanged apart from one enum match per guard call
and one `Option` check per table get.  Intended to keep every record bit-identical outside timing.
